# Suppressions for the trivy-fs gate of the central "Security Scan" required
# workflow (ContextualWisdomLab/.github, .github/workflows/security-scan.yml).
# That gate runs `trivy fs .` from the repository root with
# severity=CRITICAL,HIGH,MEDIUM and ignore-unfixed=true. Trivy picks this
# plain .trivyignore up automatically because it is the default --ignorefile;
# no trivyignores:/TRIVY_IGNOREFILE wiring exists (or is needed) in this repo.
#
# Contract for every entry (enforced by tests/test_fuzzing_integration.py):
# the comment block directly above an entry must name the rule/CVE id, the
# affected artifact, why it cannot be fixed here, and a revisit condition.
# Only add an entry after reproducing the finding from the trivy-fs job log
# (the job prints a findings table on failure) or the uploaded trivy-fs SARIF
# in code scanning. Prefer fixing (dependency bump, Dockerfile change) over
# suppressing, and rebase stale branches onto develop before concluding that
# a repo-wide finding is real.

# DS-0002 applies to .clusterfuzzlite/Dockerfile, which is a CI-only OSS-Fuzz
# builder image. ClusterFuzzLite mounts /github/workspace/build-out as a
# root-owned volume and its build harness writes libFuzzer artifacts before
# invoking the project build script, so forcing a non-root USER breaks fuzz CI.
# Revisit by 2026-10-31 or when ClusterFuzzLite supports non-root build output.
DS-0002

# CVE-2026-61632 affects pymdown-extensions, a docs-only dev dependency pulled in
# transitively by mkdocs-material and never shipped in the runtime API image
# (Dockerfile installs only the API deps). The fix lands in pymdown-extensions
# 11.x, which requires mkdocs-material >= 9.7; this repository deliberately holds
# mkdocs-material at < 9.7 (test_docs_theme_range_stays_below_warning_release and
# the documented docs-toolchain hold in CONTRIBUTING.md) because 9.7 introduces
# warnings that break `mkdocs build --strict`. mkdocs-material 9.6.x caps
# pymdown-extensions at ~=10.2 (< 11), so the CVE cannot be remediated here
# without lifting that documented hold, which is a separate migration decision.
# Revisit when the docs-toolchain hold is lifted (mkdocs-material >= 9.7 adopted,
# enabling pymdown-extensions 11) or by 2026-10-31.
CVE-2026-61632
